# UXP build outputs. The Windows native addon (uxp/win/x64/*.uxpaddon) IS
# committed — it is the artifact build-ccx.js packages, and rebuilding a static
# FFmpeg on every CI run for a file that changes twice a year is not worth it.
#
# The macOS addon is NOT committed: it cannot be built on the Windows dev
# machine, so CI builds it from source on every release and the .ccx assembles
# all three platform slices there. Anything under uxp/mac/ is a local build.
uxp/mac/
uxp/dist/
uxp/native/build/
uxp/native/uxp/win/build/
uxp/native/third_party/
uxp/ffmpeg-out/
